WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.000
STREAMING AI STARTER — EDITED SCREENSHOT WALKTHROUGH
Held frames of actual synthetic replay. No AI model is invoked.

00:15.000 --> 00:30.000
Customer story: developers need a repeatable way to explore AI interfaces
without assembling presentation, streaming, and hosting from scratch.

00:30.000 --> 00:45.000
The useful outcome is a draft handoff for human review.
This is not telemetry, diagnosis, or an autonomous equipment assistant.

00:45.000 --> 01:05.000
Command discovery: /help explains controls; /clear resets the conversation.
Keyboard autocomplete also works in the fictional experience.

01:05.000 --> 01:30.000
Replay is deliberately labeled and ignores free-form requests.
For live AI, disable replay and configure Copilot access on the host.

01:30.000 --> 01:50.000
Load the synthetic request: SYN-PUMP-042, warning W17,
vibration elevated, temperature unknown.

01:50.000 --> 02:15.000
Submit supplied context and sample procedure SYN-RUNBOOK-01.
Record observations and request duty engineer review; do not change equipment.

02:15.000 --> 02:40.000
Read FACTS and UNKNOWNS separately.
The fixed replay demonstrates the expected structure, not model quality.

02:40.000 --> 03:00.000
Select Draft handoff to demonstrate the next interaction.
In live mode, bounded conversation history accompanies each request.

03:00.000 --> 03:15.000
Inspect OWNER and NEXT ACTION.
No ticket has been filed and no equipment action has been executed.

03:15.000 --> 03:35.000
Compare the draft with the supplied procedure, then acknowledge review.
Copy for human review is a manual transfer, not an approval system.

03:35.000 --> 03:50.000
Recovery check: a deliberately interrupted network request fails visibly.
Partial or failed responses must not be mistaken for completed work.

03:50.000 --> 04:15.000
Restore connectivity and retry the same synthetic request.
The input is retained after failure; no incident was filed.

04:15.000 --> 04:35.000
Architecture: browser → Next.js API → Copilot SDK/CLI → model service.
Replay bypasses the SDK and model. Azure hosts the container, not the model.

04:35.000 --> 04:50.000
Hosted access requires a separate demo token and restricted ingress.
Azure deployment identity and runtime Copilot credentials are separate.

04:50.000 --> 05:00.000
Next step: nominate a workflow owner and three anonymized examples.
Agree authoritative context, human approval, and pilot acceptance criteria.
